# A 4x2 grid on paper, cells 64 px wide, circles of radius 20. Several fx sit on one node and run in written order, so swapping two lines changes the picture.
# Top row, left to right:
# 1. fx blur 4 then outline 4 in dark ink: the blue body is soft at its edge but the ring around it is crisp and dark.
# 2. fx outline 4 then blur 4: the ring is blurred along with the body, so the whole circle is a soft blue disc with a blurry dark halo and no crisp edge.
# 3. fx rim 6 dir:1,1 in gold, then adjust hue:120: the body is red (hue shifted from blue) and the lower-right rim band is shifted too, so it reads teal.
# 4. fx adjust hue:120, then rim 6 dir:1,1 in gold: the body is the same red, and the lower-right rim band stays gold-orange because it was added after the shift.
# Bottom row, left to right:
# 5. fx shadow 6,6 in red then adjust sat:-1: the green circle is gray and its shadow, down and right, is gray too, with no red.
# 6. fx adjust sat:-1 then shadow 6,6 in red: the circle is gray and its shadow, down and right, stays red.
@target fx/order.png 256x128

circle 20 at:32,32 fill:p.blue
  fx blur 4
  fx outline 4 color:p.ink
circle 20 at:96,32 fill:p.blue
  fx outline 4 color:p.ink
  fx blur 4
circle 20 at:160,32 fill:p.blue
  fx rim 6 dir:1,1 color:p.gold a:1
  fx adjust hue:120
circle 20 at:224,32 fill:p.blue
  fx adjust hue:120
  fx rim 6 dir:1,1 color:p.gold a:1
circle 20 at:32,96 fill:p.green
  fx shadow 6,6 blur:2 color:p.red a:1
  fx adjust sat:-1
circle 20 at:96,96 fill:p.green
  fx adjust sat:-1
  fx shadow 6,6 blur:2 color:p.red a:1
